    id: "promotions", number: "05", title: "Cadet Promotions", icon: "↑", time: "20 min",
    description: "Explore the Phase I progression from Cadet Airman Basic through the Wright Brothers Award.",
    sections: [
      { title: "Phase I: The Learning Phase", kicker: "Build foundations", body: ["Phase I introduces followership, self-discipline, CAP knowledge, drill, fitness, character, and aerospace. New cadets begin as Cadet Airman Basic and advance by completing achievement requirements and demonstrating readiness for greater responsibility.", "Promotion is more than passing online tests. Participation, performance, character, fitness, drill, and command approval all matter under the current cadet program rules."], takeaway: "Own your progress and ask staff which requirement comes next." },
      { title: "Curry Achievement", kicker: "Achievement 1 · C/Amn", body: ["The Curry Achievement is named for Maj Gen John F. Curry, CAP's first national commander. Completion earns the grade of Cadet Airman and marks the first promotion.", "Typical categories include introductory leadership learning, character participation, fitness participation, active participation, the Cadet Oath, and the required drill performance. Confirm the current checklist in the Cadet Super Chart and eServices."], takeaway: "Curry proves you can begin building reliable cadet habits." },
      { title: "Arnold & Feik", kicker: "Achievements 2–3", body: ["The Arnold Achievement honors Gen Henry H. 'Hap' Arnold and leads to Cadet Airman First Class. The Feik Achievement honors aviation pioneer and CAP leader Mary Feik and leads to Cadet Senior Airman.", "Each achievement continues leadership, aerospace, character, fitness, drill, active participation, and time-in-grade requirements as shown on the current Super Chart. Exact test modules and standards can change, so verify before planning."], takeaway: "Phase I alternates learning, practice, and increasing responsibility." },
      { title: "Wright Brothers Award", kicker: "Milestone · C/SSgt", body: ["The Wright Brothers Award marks completion of Phase I and promotion to Cadet Staff Sergeant when all current requirements are completed and the promotion is approved.", "It includes controlled milestone testing and a drill and ceremonies performance component. Milestone exams are administered through the squadron under current CAP procedures. The award also opens Phase II, where cadets begin serving as NCOs and leading teams."], takeaway: "The first milestone marks the shift from learning followership to practicing NCO leadership." },
      { title: "Plan your next promotion", kicker: "One requirement at a time", body: ["Open eServices and the current Cadet Super Chart before planning. Identify the exact leadership or aerospace module, drill test, fitness participation, character requirement, time-in-grade date, and any special requirement associated with the achievement.", "Ask staff early how your squadron schedules drill tests, milestone exams, promotion reviews, and approvals. Completing an online task at the last minute does not guarantee every in-person requirement can be administered that night.", "Keep a simple checklist with the source and completion date for each item. Continue participating and practicing after the boxes are checked—the purpose of promotion is readiness for greater responsibility, not merely collecting grade."], steps: ["Check eServices and the current Super Chart", "List every academic and in-person requirement", "Confirm the earliest eligibility date", "Schedule drill or milestone testing", "Ask for feedback before the promotion review", "Verify the promotion posted correctly"], takeaway: "Plan from official requirements, schedule early, and build the skill behind the grade." }
    ],
